1
00:00:07,560 --> 00:00:08,920
SAY NO TO PIRACY, SUPPORT ORIGINALS

2
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:44,160
If he didn't want something from you,

3
00:01:44,240 --> 00:01:48,680
why would he be so nice
as to teach you Spanish?

4
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:52,240
What could he possibly want from me?

5
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:59,040
You're overthinking it.

6
00:02:06,040 --> 00:02:07,080
Just overthinking it.

7
00:02:09,680 --> 00:02:10,639
Overthinking it.

8
00:02:13,560 --> 00:02:14,880
What's going on?

9
00:02:16,680 --> 00:02:17,760
Wait, wait.

10
00:02:17,840 --> 00:02:18,880
Come on.

11
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:20,960
What did I say?

12
00:02:27,320 --> 00:02:28,240
Alright, alright. Here, like this.

13
00:02:28,320 --> 00:02:29,840
You turn around. Turn around.

14
00:02:29,920 --> 00:02:31,360
Someone might see you.

15
00:02:33,840 --> 00:02:34,840
I'll shield you.

16
00:02:36,400 --> 00:02:37,960
Ten more seconds.

17
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:43,000
I'm good.

18
00:02:46,920 --> 00:02:47,880
Oh my God.

19
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:50,520
So embarrassing.

20
00:02:50,600 --> 00:02:52,840
People will think I'm bullying you.

21
00:02:54,320 --> 00:02:56,720
I don't cry in front of others.

22
00:02:57,800 --> 00:03:00,080
But with you… Ugh. What's this?

23
00:03:00,160 --> 00:03:01,000
Touch up your makeup.

24
00:03:01,520 --> 00:03:03,400
So I'm supposed to thank you?

25
00:03:04,480 --> 00:03:05,960
We barely ate anything.

26
00:03:12,640 --> 00:03:13,480
Missy.

27
00:03:14,440 --> 00:03:16,920
That's not how you do it. You pat it on.

28
00:03:21,320 --> 00:03:22,360
Give it here.

29
00:03:26,920 --> 00:03:30,240
I used to be wary of Ye Xinzhi.

30
00:03:30,840 --> 00:03:33,760
But seeing you now,
I'm guessing you've cleared things up?

31
00:03:34,360 --> 00:03:36,840
A single guy with his history

32
00:03:36,920 --> 00:03:39,640
and a simple girl like you
are on different paths.

33
00:03:40,240 --> 00:03:42,520
It's better for both of you
to draw the line early.

34
00:03:47,960 --> 00:03:49,000
Hold it back.

35
00:03:51,080 --> 00:03:52,160
Do you like him that much?

36
00:03:52,240 --> 00:03:53,480
I don't like him.

37
00:03:53,560 --> 00:03:55,120
I just…

38
00:04:06,400 --> 00:04:08,920
I just had a little crush.

39
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:10,120
I only saved one photo.

40
00:04:10,200 --> 00:04:12,200
Is that not allowed?
Do I have to be warned for that?

41
00:04:15,560 --> 00:04:19,839
Listen, this is just
a passing infatuation.

42
00:04:19,920 --> 00:04:21,120
In less than two months,

43
00:04:21,200 --> 00:04:23,720
when you look back on him,
the spell will break.

44
00:04:23,800 --> 00:04:27,120
You'll think you were so silly.

45
00:04:27,720 --> 00:04:30,800
I figured it out while crying just now.

46
00:04:30,880 --> 00:04:32,960
What matters most to me right now
is my career.

47
00:04:33,040 --> 00:04:34,840
With a career, I can have any man I want.

48
00:04:34,920 --> 00:04:37,560
So after this Bolo Culture deal is done,

49
00:04:37,640 --> 00:04:39,280
I'll apply to Sha Sha.

50
00:04:39,360 --> 00:04:41,440
I want to go after
digital finance clients.

51
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:43,880
Digital finance?

52
00:04:45,840 --> 00:04:47,280
He told me that too.

53
00:04:47,360 --> 00:04:48,560
When choosing industries,

54
00:04:48,640 --> 00:04:50,360
you have to find ones
with money and orders.

55
00:04:50,880 --> 00:04:52,240
If your first project

56
00:04:52,320 --> 00:04:55,920
wasn't an internet unicorn
like Bolo Culture,

57
00:04:56,480 --> 00:04:58,080
you wouldn't be standing here.

58
00:04:58,920 --> 00:05:00,840
He said if you want to last in consulting,

59
00:05:00,920 --> 00:05:03,760
you have to choose industries with
big budgets and strong growth potential.

60
00:05:08,960 --> 00:05:10,200
Eat up.

61
00:05:12,920 --> 00:05:14,240
Eat.

62
00:05:24,480 --> 00:05:26,040
Need to drop another 5,000.

63
00:05:27,160 --> 00:05:28,680
Five thousand…

64
00:05:29,520 --> 00:05:31,240
Five thousand's still not enough.
At least 10,000.

65
00:05:31,320 --> 00:05:32,160
AVERAGE TRANSACTION PRICE

66
00:05:33,240 --> 00:05:34,480
Are you buying an apartment?

67
00:05:36,200 --> 00:05:37,800
No, no. Just browsing.

68
00:05:38,400 --> 00:05:40,000
If you are buying, let me know.

69
00:05:40,080 --> 00:05:41,840
I'm a big client at their bank.

70
00:05:41,920 --> 00:05:44,360
I can put in a word
and get you the best rate.

71
00:05:44,440 --> 00:05:45,520
Really?

72
00:05:45,600 --> 00:05:48,040
No, no. I couldn't possibly.

73
00:05:48,120 --> 00:05:50,040
It's nothing. Just a fraction
of a percent on the rate.

74
00:05:50,120 --> 00:05:50,960
It's no big deal.

75
00:05:51,720 --> 00:05:54,080
Actually, I need a favor today.

76
00:05:54,160 --> 00:05:56,200
I had a fender bender with Lin Long.

77
00:05:56,280 --> 00:05:57,520
I took full responsibility,

78
00:05:57,600 --> 00:05:59,000
but it's a bit complicated.

79
00:05:59,080 --> 00:06:01,040
My car insurance is from out of town.

80
00:06:01,120 --> 00:06:03,040
I need her to sign off on something.

81
00:06:04,040 --> 00:06:06,040
Sure. I'll take care of it for you.

82
00:06:08,560 --> 00:06:10,960
I heard Lin Long's been having
a rough time lately?

83
00:06:15,320 --> 00:06:16,840
Give this to her.

84
00:06:16,920 --> 00:06:19,400
I went to Baiyun Temple the other day
and got one for everyone at the company.

85
00:06:20,360 --> 00:06:22,880
She was the one
who started this project after all.

86
00:06:23,480 --> 00:06:24,640
Just tell her I wish her

87
00:06:26,080 --> 00:06:28,000
a rebirth through hardship
and better days ahead.

88
00:06:29,560 --> 00:06:30,760
Sure.

89
00:06:31,600 --> 00:06:33,600
I started the project too. Where's mine?

90
00:06:38,280 --> 00:06:39,600
Don't you have your "senior"?

91
00:06:43,640 --> 00:06:44,720
I shouldn't have said that.

92
00:06:47,080 --> 00:06:49,680
Rebirth through hardship and better days?

93
00:06:50,800 --> 00:06:54,160
A client I've only known for a few days
sends me good wishes,

94
00:06:54,240 --> 00:06:58,760
but my legal husband
only has the cruelest words for me.

95
00:06:59,440 --> 00:07:00,320
Did he come after you?

96
00:07:00,920 --> 00:07:01,880
No.

97
00:07:01,960 --> 00:07:03,560
He just realized I didn't go home,

98
00:07:03,640 --> 00:07:05,400
moved straight
to the postpartum care center instead.

99
00:07:05,480 --> 00:07:07,040
And I changed my bank card PIN,

100
00:07:07,120 --> 00:07:08,880
so he figured out I want a divorce.

101
00:07:08,960 --> 00:07:11,600
He's got all our relatives and friends

102
00:07:11,680 --> 00:07:16,320
texting me, telling me
to come to my senses.

103
00:07:19,800 --> 00:07:21,960
I didn't get you a fruit basket.

104
00:07:22,480 --> 00:07:24,920
I picked out the newest shade of lipstick.

105
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:26,520
It'll brighten up your complexion.

106
00:07:26,600 --> 00:07:30,200
Whether you end up
at the Civil Affairs Bureau or court,

107
00:07:30,280 --> 00:07:31,600
you won't look like you're losing.

108
00:07:35,600 --> 00:07:36,760
Look at you.

109
00:07:37,280 --> 00:07:39,680
Such a thoughtful girl. What--

110
00:07:39,760 --> 00:07:42,840
What was wrong with me back then?
Why did I have to push you out?

111
00:07:46,040 --> 00:07:48,560
I was a bit too aggressive, too.

112
00:07:49,440 --> 00:07:50,600
Sir, you can't go in.

113
00:07:50,680 --> 00:07:52,480
You can't go in, sir.

114
00:07:52,560 --> 00:07:54,560
I'm her husband! Why can't I go in?

115
00:07:54,640 --> 00:07:56,240
She's weak right now.

116
00:07:56,320 --> 00:07:57,840
It's fine. Let him in.

117
00:08:02,120 --> 00:08:03,760
How much longer
are you going to act crazy?

118
00:08:04,360 --> 00:08:05,680
Come home with me.

119
00:08:05,760 --> 00:08:06,800
Let go of me.

120
00:08:08,040 --> 00:08:08,960
Let go of me!

121
00:08:09,480 --> 00:08:10,400
Let… Let go…

122
00:08:14,440 --> 00:08:15,560
Jiang Zhiwen, listen to me.

123
00:08:16,240 --> 00:08:17,400
You can refuse to divorce,

124
00:08:17,480 --> 00:08:19,040
but I've already consulted a lawyer.

125
00:08:19,120 --> 00:08:21,120
You pushed me and caused a miscarriage.

126
00:08:21,200 --> 00:08:23,160
That counts as slight bodily injury.
You'll be held criminally liable.

127
00:08:23,840 --> 00:08:26,080
Believe me, if I press charges,

128
00:08:26,160 --> 00:08:30,840
your career will be ruined,
and if you remarry and have children,

129
00:08:30,920 --> 00:08:32,679
their background checks
for school and employment

130
00:08:32,760 --> 00:08:34,200
will always be an issue.

131
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:36,559
I have video proof of you hitting her.

132
00:08:36,640 --> 00:08:38,000
When did you see me hit her?

133
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:48,160
You two set me up, didn't you?

134
00:08:54,520 --> 00:08:55,600
Jiang Zhiwen.

135
00:08:56,560 --> 00:08:57,760
Let's get a divorce.

136
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:01,680
Let's both keep some dignity.

137
00:09:02,560 --> 00:09:04,120
You want a divorce?

138
00:09:04,720 --> 00:09:05,760
Fine.

139
00:09:05,840 --> 00:09:07,880
Cash goes to you.
The apartment goes to me!

140
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:15,920
Oh, and there's a fund maturing soon.

141
00:09:16,440 --> 00:09:17,760
That gets split equally!

142
00:09:19,240 --> 00:09:20,280
Get out!

143
00:09:22,760 --> 00:09:23,720
You crazy woman!

144
00:09:25,680 --> 00:09:27,360
I paid two-thirds
of the down payment on that apartment.

145
00:09:27,440 --> 00:09:28,640
I've paid more
on the mortgage than him, too.

146
00:09:28,720 --> 00:09:30,160
Why should the apartment go to him?

147
00:09:30,240 --> 00:09:32,480
The moment I'm discharged,
I'm filing for divorce.

148
00:09:32,560 --> 00:09:34,840
Ms. Huang told me
I can use that soon-to-mature trust

149
00:09:34,920 --> 00:09:37,680
to buy jewelry or designer bags.

150
00:09:37,760 --> 00:09:39,600
That way, they count as personal items

151
00:09:39,680 --> 00:09:41,200
and don't get split
in the property division.

152
00:09:42,320 --> 00:09:46,960
But isn't buying millions
in jewelry all at once a bit much?

153
00:09:47,040 --> 00:09:48,520
Would the court even accept that?

154
00:09:48,600 --> 00:09:50,520
There is a risk.

155
00:09:50,600 --> 00:09:52,960
But there's no better solution for now.

156
00:09:59,480 --> 00:10:00,880
Remember Fushun Insurance Group,
the one that handles

157
00:10:00,960 --> 00:10:02,520
our corporate medical insurance?

158
00:10:02,600 --> 00:10:06,000
I've been looking into digital finance
in the insurance sector lately,

159
00:10:06,080 --> 00:10:08,520
so I asked them for some materials.

160
00:10:08,600 --> 00:10:10,320
There was a marketing case study in there.

161
00:10:11,120 --> 00:10:14,880
Look. It says that according to the law,
the cash value of an insurance policy

162
00:10:14,960 --> 00:10:16,560
is considered marital property,

163
00:10:16,640 --> 00:10:19,680
but the insurance contract itself
belongs to the policyholder.

164
00:10:19,760 --> 00:10:22,320
I think you could ask a broker in Fushun

165
00:10:22,400 --> 00:10:24,960
to find you a short-to-medium-term policy

166
00:10:25,040 --> 00:10:26,720
with very low cash value
in the first two years.

167
00:10:27,560 --> 00:10:30,440
Say, only 10% of the total coverage?

168
00:10:30,520 --> 00:10:32,800
That way, after the divorce,
you only have to give him 5%.

169
00:10:32,880 --> 00:10:36,000
But when the contract matures,
you still get the full payout,

170
00:10:36,080 --> 00:10:38,200
plus decent returns.

171
00:10:38,280 --> 00:10:39,320
That's great.

172
00:10:39,400 --> 00:10:41,680
I'll check with my lawyer later
to see if this works.

173
00:10:41,760 --> 00:10:43,280
Okay. I'll send this over to you.

174
00:10:44,240 --> 00:10:45,880
- Thanks.
- No problem.

175
00:10:47,160 --> 00:10:48,280
Really, thank you.

176
00:10:51,040 --> 00:10:53,920
Think of it as my apology

177
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:56,120
for causing that fight between you two
at Wanghu Pavilion Restaurant.

178
00:10:56,640 --> 00:10:57,520
Don't even bring that up.

179
00:10:57,600 --> 00:10:59,840
What I did was awful.

180
00:10:59,920 --> 00:11:02,920
Personally, I hate it when men
make unwanted advances at work.

181
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:03,880
But I--

182
00:11:03,960 --> 00:11:05,240
We said we'd wipe the slate clean.

183
00:11:37,240 --> 00:11:38,920
FINTECH DEVELOPMENT

184
00:11:50,720 --> 00:11:51,480
Ms. Sha…

185
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:57,480
Still researching digital finance?

186
00:11:58,120 --> 00:11:59,080
You really want to do this?

187
00:12:01,640 --> 00:12:04,920
You want advanced access to the company's
digital finance database?

188
00:12:06,400 --> 00:12:08,400
Looks like your workload
isn't heavy enough.

189
00:12:09,280 --> 00:12:11,760
I can always make time.

190
00:12:11,840 --> 00:12:14,240
I just want to learn as much as I can.

191
00:12:14,320 --> 00:12:16,280
Maxmise isn't a training center.

192
00:12:16,360 --> 00:12:18,520
The HR Statistical Yearbook says

193
00:12:18,600 --> 00:12:21,280
the first year is when new hires
learn the fastest.

194
00:12:21,360 --> 00:12:23,640
Well, you gave me a chance
on the Bolo Culture project.

195
00:12:23,720 --> 00:12:26,160
Maybe I can create even more value
for the company in the future.

196
00:12:26,240 --> 00:12:29,200
Ms. Sha, don't you love
ambitious subordinates?

197
00:12:31,520 --> 00:12:32,360
I'll think about it.

198
00:12:36,400 --> 00:12:37,880
Ma Ke has completed
his strategic hypothesis

199
00:12:37,960 --> 00:12:39,800
for Celestial Insurance's
digital transformation.

200
00:12:39,880 --> 00:12:42,000
They're in the strategy testing phase now.

201
00:12:42,080 --> 00:12:45,120
If you want, you can transfer
to that team soon.

202
00:12:45,920 --> 00:12:49,000
But your bonus on the Bolo Culture project
only runs through this week.

203
00:12:49,880 --> 00:12:51,680
I'd love to. Of course I would.

204
00:12:52,280 --> 00:12:56,680
But would it look bad
if I left in the middle of a project?

205
00:12:56,760 --> 00:12:58,800
One person less
won't affect the project's progress.

206
00:12:59,560 --> 00:13:03,160
Since Ye Xinzhi said
you're an explorer type,

207
00:13:03,240 --> 00:13:05,480
I'm willing to give you
a chance to transfer.

208
00:13:06,400 --> 00:13:08,960
Is it just because of him?

209
00:13:09,040 --> 00:13:10,440
Of course not.

210
00:13:10,520 --> 00:13:14,640
It's because you're smart, capable,
and hard-working enough.

211
00:13:16,480 --> 00:13:20,480
Lin Long told me
about the insurance advice you gave her.

212
00:13:20,560 --> 00:13:21,480
I think you have talent.

213
00:13:23,400 --> 00:13:24,520
Thank you, Ms. Sha.

214
00:13:25,880 --> 00:13:26,800
Alright.

215
00:13:27,320 --> 00:13:28,560
Go home and get some rest.

216
00:13:28,640 --> 00:13:29,560
Your health is yours alone.

217
00:13:30,480 --> 00:13:33,040
If you fall, someone
will replace you immediately.

218
00:13:33,880 --> 00:13:36,000
I'll make sure to exercise
and won't let that happen.

219
00:13:38,440 --> 00:13:39,640
- Bye.
- See you tomorrow.

220
00:13:53,120 --> 00:13:56,840
Ms. Lu said she hasn't found
a suitable place yet,

221
00:13:56,920 --> 00:13:59,480
so I asked an agent I know.

222
00:13:59,560 --> 00:14:02,880
This place is only three subway stations
from the office.

223
00:14:02,960 --> 00:14:04,080
Rent is reasonable too.

224
00:14:04,160 --> 00:14:05,200
MOM AND BABY IN GOOD HANDS
FAMILY CAN REST EASY

225
00:14:05,280 --> 00:14:06,120
Take a look.

226
00:14:06,960 --> 00:14:07,840
- Okay. Thanks.
- Just put it here.

227
00:14:07,920 --> 00:14:09,040
Sure.

228
00:14:09,920 --> 00:14:11,120
What do you think?

229
00:14:11,200 --> 00:14:13,200
I've rented in this complex before.

230
00:14:13,280 --> 00:14:14,680
It's good. No issues.

231
00:14:15,800 --> 00:14:18,240
Send me the agent's contact info later.

232
00:14:18,320 --> 00:14:19,680
I'll put down the deposit first.

233
00:14:21,240 --> 00:14:23,720
If you're comfortable with it,
give me your ID.

234
00:14:23,800 --> 00:14:25,080
I'll handle the paperwork for you.

235
00:14:25,680 --> 00:14:26,800
You haven't fully recovered yet.

236
00:14:26,880 --> 00:14:28,320
I'll take care of it for you.

237
00:14:28,400 --> 00:14:29,520
That would be great.

238
00:14:31,120 --> 00:14:32,440
But can you manage?

239
00:14:32,520 --> 00:14:35,800
Didn't you just start
on the Bolo Culture project?

240
00:14:36,440 --> 00:14:39,600
I transferred to Ma Ke's
Celestial Insurance project.

241
00:14:41,120 --> 00:14:42,720
Don't worry. I wasn't pushed out.

242
00:14:42,800 --> 00:14:46,320
I applied myself
because I wanted to try digital finance.

243
00:14:47,760 --> 00:14:50,280
I actually came by today
to let you know this.

244
00:14:51,280 --> 00:14:55,600
After all, you were the one
who took me to pitch Bolo Culture.

245
00:14:57,680 --> 00:14:58,680
True.

246
00:14:58,760 --> 00:15:01,800
Remember how we fought
tooth and nail over this project?

247
00:15:01,880 --> 00:15:04,120
And now neither of us is on it.

248
00:15:05,720 --> 00:15:08,960
Ma Ke can be a bit tricky.

249
00:15:09,040 --> 00:15:10,560
Keep your guard up.

250
00:15:11,200 --> 00:15:12,560
Okay. Got it.

251
00:15:13,080 --> 00:15:14,040
Don't worry about me.

252
00:15:14,120 --> 00:15:16,000
Your top priority
is to get your health back.

253
00:15:17,520 --> 00:15:20,000
Don't take this the wrong way.

254
00:15:21,240 --> 00:15:22,960
But there's one thing
I've never understood.

255
00:15:23,040 --> 00:15:25,640
What did you ever see
in a man like Jiang Zhiwen?

256
00:15:27,600 --> 00:15:30,440
Back then, I was much like you.

257
00:15:30,520 --> 00:15:31,640
I had just joined Maxmise.

258
00:15:32,160 --> 00:15:36,800
I was busy, exhausted,
and lonely every day.

259
00:15:36,880 --> 00:15:39,880
So it was easy to reach
for whatever warmth

260
00:15:40,920 --> 00:15:42,680
was within arm's reach.

261
00:15:46,600 --> 00:15:47,560
Good luck.

262
00:15:57,600 --> 00:15:59,520
Then why did you teach me
how to pick restaurants?

263
00:16:00,120 --> 00:16:01,640
Most people don't need to be taught that.

264
00:16:02,240 --> 00:16:04,720
I told you not to drink recklessly.

265
00:16:04,800 --> 00:16:07,000
Besides, I am here.

266
00:16:12,560 --> 00:16:16,040
<i>Warmth within arm's reach.</i>

267
00:16:20,880 --> 00:16:22,640
I've organized all the materials
on Benyuan Digital Collectibles.

268
00:16:22,720 --> 00:16:24,640
The key points are marked in highlighter.

269
00:16:27,480 --> 00:16:28,840
How are you settling
into the new project team?

270
00:16:30,400 --> 00:16:31,440
Pretty good.

271
00:16:32,240 --> 00:16:33,560
The project manager guiding me
is named Ma Ke.

272
00:16:33,640 --> 00:16:34,720
He's nice.

273
00:16:34,800 --> 00:16:37,040
He's already let me work
on designing solutions.

274
00:16:37,120 --> 00:16:38,160
And Yang Rui.

275
00:16:38,240 --> 00:16:40,440
He's teaching me
specific diagnostic techniques.

276
00:16:41,040 --> 00:16:44,040
Way more engaging than just
doing interviews and plugging into models.

277
00:16:44,680 --> 00:16:45,920
Who's Yang Rui?

278
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:47,320
You never mentioned him before.

279
00:16:47,400 --> 00:16:49,840
I thought Bu Tianna
was your only friend at Maxmise.

280
00:16:53,440 --> 00:16:54,480
Thanks.

281
00:16:54,560 --> 00:16:56,560
This trekking pole is non-slip. Take it.

282
00:16:57,080 --> 00:16:58,280
Aren't you trying to win?

283
00:16:58,360 --> 00:17:00,000
If you slip and get hurt, you can't win.

284
00:17:00,080 --> 00:17:01,400
You're a good girl,

285
00:17:01,480 --> 00:17:03,920
and I hate seeing people
take advantage of you.

286
00:17:04,440 --> 00:17:06,280
Of course not.

287
00:17:06,800 --> 00:17:09,480
I hang out with colleagues all the time.

288
00:17:09,560 --> 00:17:10,800
See?

289
00:17:12,880 --> 00:17:13,760
Look.

290
00:17:14,280 --> 00:17:15,599
Us.

291
00:17:15,680 --> 00:17:16,680
This is Yang Rui.

292
00:17:16,760 --> 00:17:19,079
A buddy who's helped me out a lot.

293
00:17:19,160 --> 00:17:20,480
He's already a consultant.

294
00:17:20,560 --> 00:17:22,119
See? And this.

295
00:17:22,760 --> 00:17:23,599
DANCE BUDDY READY

296
00:17:24,200 --> 00:17:25,560
That's the two of us dancing.

297
00:17:26,720 --> 00:17:28,960
I think Shen Jin sent me that.

298
00:17:29,480 --> 00:17:30,560
Funny, huh?

299
00:17:30,640 --> 00:17:32,280
Look at your face.

300
00:17:32,360 --> 00:17:34,160
So funny. Is it funny?

301
00:17:34,800 --> 00:17:35,840
Yeah.

302
00:17:40,720 --> 00:17:41,560
Here.

303
00:17:41,640 --> 00:17:44,200
Let me teach you the Bottom-Up BPR method.

304
00:17:44,280 --> 00:17:45,120
You'll definitely need it later.

305
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:53,840
Why are you staring at me?

306
00:17:55,040 --> 00:17:56,240
Nothing, nothing.

307
00:17:57,600 --> 00:17:58,840
What do you mean, nothing?

308
00:17:59,520 --> 00:18:00,520
Just say it.

309
00:18:07,800 --> 00:18:09,080
You look so worn out lately.

310
00:18:09,160 --> 00:18:10,720
Your dark circles are really bad,

311
00:18:10,800 --> 00:18:12,440
and the lines around your eyes
are so deep.

312
00:18:13,480 --> 00:18:14,960
- I've been staying up late lately.
- Right?

313
00:18:15,040 --> 00:18:16,160
Everyone can tell your energy's off.

314
00:18:16,240 --> 00:18:17,920
That won't do.

315
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:20,320
How about this? I'll get you a thermos.

316
00:18:20,400 --> 00:18:22,760
You can steep some goji berries
and cassia seeds in it.

317
00:18:22,840 --> 00:18:24,400
It's really good for you. Seriously.

318
00:18:25,040 --> 00:18:26,240
No more coffee for you.

319
00:18:26,320 --> 00:18:27,640
Your blood is basically coffee.

320
00:18:27,720 --> 00:18:28,560
How about some goji berries?

321
00:18:30,240 --> 00:18:31,360
I'll order it right now.

322
00:18:32,480 --> 00:18:35,600
Well, goji berries.

323
00:18:35,680 --> 00:18:37,280
Gotta take care of yourself
as you get older.

324
00:18:37,360 --> 00:18:38,520
Otherwise, it's no good.

325
00:18:38,600 --> 00:18:40,920
I'll get the biggest thermos.

326
00:18:41,760 --> 00:18:42,840
Thanks.

327
00:18:43,480 --> 00:18:44,680
No worries.

328
00:18:48,480 --> 00:18:50,840
I won this round.

329
00:18:50,920 --> 00:18:53,800
He must be thinking that what he did
that day was totally unnecessary

330
00:18:53,880 --> 00:18:55,000
and presumptuous.

331
00:18:55,080 --> 00:18:55,920
<i>Nice one.</i>

332
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:57,360
The key was that phrase "worn out".

333
00:18:57,440 --> 00:18:58,800
<i>A single "you're outdated"</i>

334
00:18:58,880 --> 00:19:01,760
was enough to shred
their pathetic confidence.

335
00:19:02,680 --> 00:19:03,880
Yeah.

336
00:19:03,960 --> 00:19:06,440
His face was hilarious.
I wish I could've taken a picture for you.

337
00:19:06,520 --> 00:19:08,720
<i>He shouldn't have chosen that way</i>
<i>to crush my self-esteem.</i>

338
00:19:10,280 --> 00:19:12,080
MA KE FROM MAXMISE

339
00:19:13,840 --> 00:19:16,160
I gotta go. Ma Ke is calling me.

340
00:19:16,240 --> 00:19:17,280
<i>Wait.</i>

341
00:19:17,360 --> 00:19:18,720
<i>- There's something I want to tell you.</i>
- What is it?

342
00:19:24,360 --> 00:19:25,480
Never mind.

343
00:19:25,560 --> 00:19:26,880
I'll tell you some other time.

344
00:19:36,200 --> 00:19:39,160
Sorry. I was on a call. What do you need?

345
00:19:39,240 --> 00:19:40,920
Bu Tianna is joining our project team.

346
00:19:41,760 --> 00:19:42,800
You two are close.

347
00:19:43,440 --> 00:19:45,080
<i>I'll leave it to you to get her</i>
<i>up to speed on the project.</i>

348
00:19:46,440 --> 00:19:47,360
<i>Any issues?</i>

349
00:19:47,880 --> 00:19:48,800
Okay.

350
00:19:51,200 --> 00:19:53,360
<i>I thought Bu Tianna</i>
<i>was your only friend at Maxmise.</i>

351
00:19:54,520 --> 00:19:58,000
Your friend Bu Tianna
is the one with the real connections.

352
00:20:00,080 --> 00:20:01,520
<i>After this Bolo Culture deal is done,</i>

353
00:20:01,600 --> 00:20:03,840
<i>I'll go after digital finance clients.</i>

354
00:20:03,920 --> 00:20:04,800
Digital finance?

355
00:20:05,600 --> 00:20:07,600
He said if you want to last in consulting,

356
00:20:07,680 --> 00:20:10,920
you have to choose industries with
big budgets and strong growth potential.

357
00:20:24,640 --> 00:20:25,560
It's about Bu Tianna, right?

358
00:20:27,800 --> 00:20:30,800
I was right there when she talked
to Mr. Pi yesterday.

359
00:20:30,880 --> 00:20:33,800
She said her family
is partnering with Ande Energy.

360
00:20:33,880 --> 00:20:36,080
She was worried about kickbacks
in the project,

361
00:20:36,160 --> 00:20:38,720
and she heard you say
digital finance has potential,

362
00:20:38,800 --> 00:20:40,400
so she wanted
to try switching project teams.

363
00:20:40,480 --> 00:20:41,400
With that said,

364
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:43,840
of course, Mr. Pi moved her
to the Celestial project.

365
00:20:43,920 --> 00:20:46,000
But that puts you in a tough spot.

366
00:20:48,120 --> 00:20:50,760
The Celestial project has a lot going on.

367
00:20:50,840 --> 00:20:52,400
Having more colleagues around is fine.

368
00:20:56,200 --> 00:20:57,760
Stop pretending to be calm.

369
00:20:57,840 --> 00:21:00,760
Just stay away from Bu Tianna, will you?

370
00:21:01,600 --> 00:21:03,680
You used to be so sharp.

371
00:21:03,760 --> 00:21:06,120
Why are you so naive about this?

372
00:21:06,200 --> 00:21:07,960
<i>What does someone like her,</i>
<i>born with a silver spoon,</i>

373
00:21:08,040 --> 00:21:09,240
<i>want from being close to you?</i>

374
00:21:09,320 --> 00:21:11,240
<i>Just another pair of eyes.</i>

375
00:21:13,440 --> 00:21:14,280
Where are you going?

376
00:21:14,360 --> 00:21:17,120
I said I'm delivering
a document for Deng Anran.

377
00:21:19,640 --> 00:21:20,520
Did I hear that right?

378
00:21:20,600 --> 00:21:21,640
She's delivering documents for Deng Anran?

379
00:21:21,720 --> 00:21:22,880
Shouldn't she be helping Bu Tianna?

380
00:21:22,960 --> 00:21:24,280
Since when is she
so close with Deng Anran?

381
00:21:24,360 --> 00:21:25,400
You don't know?

382
00:21:25,920 --> 00:21:27,280
Bu Tianna applied to join…

383
00:21:29,440 --> 00:21:30,600
Really?

384
00:21:34,680 --> 00:21:36,640
<i>You think there are real friends</i>
<i>in the office?</i>

385
00:21:36,720 --> 00:21:39,280
<i>You think chatting and having</i>
<i>lunch together makes you besties?</i>

386
00:21:39,360 --> 00:21:41,040
Aren't you and Lin Long friends?

387
00:21:42,080 --> 00:21:43,160
We're different.

388
00:21:43,240 --> 00:21:45,680
We were college classmates
and roommates for four years.

389
00:21:45,760 --> 00:21:47,960
But I'll admit,

390
00:21:48,040 --> 00:21:50,280
if it came down to a promotion between us,

391
00:21:50,360 --> 00:21:51,880
I wouldn't hold back.

392
00:21:51,960 --> 00:21:55,240
<i>That's exactly why Lin Long</i>
<i>and Cindy can't stand each other.</i>

393
00:22:00,280 --> 00:22:01,720
<i>Why do you keep helping me?</i>

394
00:22:01,800 --> 00:22:04,960
<i>I'm going to become a partner someday.</i>

395
00:22:05,040 --> 00:22:07,320
<i>I just want to start building</i>
<i>my inner circle early.</i>

396
00:22:07,920 --> 00:22:09,360
<i>Of course, I don't care.</i>

397
00:22:10,240 --> 00:22:11,880
But don't act weak.

398
00:22:11,960 --> 00:22:13,520
Doesn't fit your image.

399
00:22:13,600 --> 00:22:17,360
I'm keeping you as my right hand,
not my friend.

400
00:22:17,440 --> 00:22:19,720
Right hand means trust.

401
00:22:19,800 --> 00:22:23,160
<i>Competition for work</i>
<i>is normal in an office.</i>

402
00:22:23,240 --> 00:22:24,520
You'll get used to it.

403
00:22:24,600 --> 00:22:27,440
In consulting, it all
comes down to ability.

404
00:22:27,520 --> 00:22:29,920
Why are you so interested in me today?

405
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:33,760
Don't tell me you're jealous
I got promoted to SBA before you?

406
00:22:34,920 --> 00:22:37,880
<i>We only met when we joined the company,</i>
<i>so why have you always been</i>

407
00:22:38,480 --> 00:22:39,400
so nice to me?

408
00:22:39,480 --> 00:22:40,760
Because I like you.

409
00:22:40,840 --> 00:22:45,400
One of the reasons I like you is that
communication with you is so efficient.

410
00:22:53,840 --> 00:22:56,600
<i>Chi. You're so good to me.</i>

411
00:22:58,080 --> 00:22:59,680
<i>You saved me that day.</i>

412
00:23:00,280 --> 00:23:02,840
I'm going to be really,
really good to you from now on.

413
00:23:02,920 --> 00:23:04,320
You turn around. Turn around.

414
00:23:04,920 --> 00:23:06,160
I'll shield you.

415
00:23:08,840 --> 00:23:11,720
YE THE LEGEND

416
00:23:11,800 --> 00:23:12,880
YE THE LEGEND MISSED CALL

417
00:23:14,640 --> 00:23:15,560
YE THE LEGEND CALLING

418
00:24:14,040 --> 00:24:15,080
<i>Sorry, Mom.</i>

419
00:24:16,200 --> 00:24:17,560
<i>I forgot what you told me.</i>

420
00:24:18,720 --> 00:24:20,360
<i>I easily trusted someone too.</i>

421
00:24:21,200 --> 00:24:23,360
<i>And now I've become their stepping stone.</i>

422
00:24:52,360 --> 00:24:55,080
Xu Chi, you haven't answered your phone
or replied to WeChat all afternoon.

423
00:24:55,160 --> 00:24:56,160
I called your company,

424
00:24:56,240 --> 00:24:57,200
and the front desk said
they couldn't reach you.

425
00:24:58,280 --> 00:24:59,440
I'm fine.

426
00:24:59,520 --> 00:25:01,600
But Du was worried about you.
He asked me to find you.

427
00:25:01,680 --> 00:25:03,120
How did you know I was here?

428
00:25:03,880 --> 00:25:06,880
I remembered you said
your mom's old apartment was around here.

429
00:25:07,480 --> 00:25:08,560
So I came to check.

430
00:25:11,000 --> 00:25:11,840
I'm fine.

431
00:25:15,440 --> 00:25:16,600
You call this fine?

432
00:25:18,080 --> 00:25:18,920
Look at yourself.

433
00:26:03,160 --> 00:26:04,000
What happened?

434
00:26:09,400 --> 00:26:10,960
I've been looking for you all afternoon.

435
00:26:11,040 --> 00:26:12,760
Just tell me. What happened?

436
00:26:12,840 --> 00:26:14,440
I don't want to talk to you, okay?

437
00:26:28,000 --> 00:26:28,920
Fine.

438
00:26:29,960 --> 00:26:31,440
Self-punishment and now self-isolation?

439
00:26:33,960 --> 00:26:35,040
I'll play along.

440
00:27:32,680 --> 00:27:34,120
- What are you doing?
- You're awake?

441
00:27:34,200 --> 00:27:36,000
- What are you doing, Ye Xinzhi?
- Relax.

442
00:27:36,080 --> 00:27:37,560
- This is a closed road.
- No cars. No people.

443
00:27:37,640 --> 00:27:39,640
- What are you doing? Stop the car!
- Hold on!

444
00:27:42,920 --> 00:27:44,040
Stop the car!

445
00:27:46,680 --> 00:27:48,760
Ye Xinzhi! What are you doing?

446
00:27:49,280 --> 00:27:50,040
Stop!

447
00:27:52,280 --> 00:27:54,160
Are you crazy? Stop the car!

448
00:28:01,800 --> 00:28:02,880
Are you insane?

449
00:28:02,960 --> 00:28:04,080
Ye Xinzhi, what are you doing?

450
00:28:12,600 --> 00:28:14,960
Did that help ease the heaviness
in your chest a little?

451
00:29:35,920 --> 00:29:36,960
Done crying?

452
00:29:39,840 --> 00:29:40,800
Sorry.

453
00:29:41,440 --> 00:29:44,880
I shouldn't have snapped at you.

454
00:29:47,120 --> 00:29:48,880
Don't apologize at a time like this.

455
00:29:49,840 --> 00:29:54,640
Getting backstabbed by someone
you trusted at work really hurts.

456
00:29:56,320 --> 00:29:57,800
You'll get used to it after a few times.

457
00:30:00,400 --> 00:30:02,320
I'm not sad.

458
00:30:02,400 --> 00:30:05,800
I just feel like such an idiot.

459
00:30:05,880 --> 00:30:07,480
Ever since my mom left,

460
00:30:07,560 --> 00:30:10,320
I swore I'd be independent and guarded.

461
00:30:10,400 --> 00:30:12,080
That I wouldn't trust or depend on anyone.

462
00:30:12,800 --> 00:30:16,320
But just because Bu Tianna
helped me a few times,

463
00:30:17,200 --> 00:30:18,720
I let my guard down.

464
00:30:18,800 --> 00:30:19,880
I even…

465
00:30:21,680 --> 00:30:23,680
I don't like him.

466
00:30:24,280 --> 00:30:25,560
I just…

467
00:30:26,560 --> 00:30:28,880
I just had a little crush.

468
00:30:28,960 --> 00:30:30,280
<i>I only saved one photo.</i>

469
00:30:30,360 --> 00:30:32,320
<i>Is that not allowed?</i>
<i>Do I have to be warned for that?</i>

470
00:30:36,680 --> 00:30:38,960
I even told her everything on my mind.

471
00:30:40,160 --> 00:30:41,480
And now here I am.

472
00:30:49,800 --> 00:30:51,040
Where are you at now?

473
00:30:52,760 --> 00:30:54,000
She just joined that project team.

474
00:30:54,080 --> 00:30:56,560
The fight hasn't even started yet,
and you're already giving up?

475
00:30:57,680 --> 00:31:01,720
Or do you think you don't even have
what it takes to compete with her?

476
00:31:03,400 --> 00:31:05,680
I don't think you're crying
because you feel stupid.

477
00:31:06,320 --> 00:31:08,680
Deep down, you're insecure.

478
00:31:09,280 --> 00:31:10,600
After all this,

479
00:31:10,680 --> 00:31:12,840
you don't even have the courage
to confront her.

480
00:31:15,760 --> 00:31:16,920
Am I right?

481
00:31:20,280 --> 00:31:21,360
Answer me.

482
00:31:31,400 --> 00:31:32,440
Yes.

483
00:31:34,240 --> 00:31:35,640
You can still answer me.

484
00:31:36,160 --> 00:31:37,120
That means there's still hope.

485
00:31:39,560 --> 00:31:40,720
Anything else you can't figure out?

486
00:31:40,800 --> 00:31:41,640
Spill it one by one.

487
00:31:41,720 --> 00:31:43,800
Full confession gets you leniency.

488
00:31:48,880 --> 00:31:49,840
Actually…

489
00:31:52,200 --> 00:31:55,960
Even though I always said
I didn't envy Bu Tianna's advantages,

490
00:31:56,040 --> 00:31:58,960
I've been avoiding
a head-to-head competition with her

491
00:31:59,040 --> 00:31:59,960
because I'm afraid of losing.

492
00:32:00,880 --> 00:32:04,520
You know, I've never lost
a competition since college,

493
00:32:04,600 --> 00:32:06,800
so I'm scared that if I lose to her,

494
00:32:07,320 --> 00:32:08,480
my perfect record will be broken.

495
00:32:09,080 --> 00:32:10,200
I don't want to be replaced.

496
00:32:15,000 --> 00:32:16,080
You know the hand-slap game?

497
00:32:19,640 --> 00:32:20,840
What for?

498
00:32:32,640 --> 00:32:34,120
You said you've never lost, right?

499
00:32:34,720 --> 00:32:35,600
I'll go.

500
00:33:01,520 --> 00:33:02,720
Lose a few times,

501
00:33:02,800 --> 00:33:05,000
and all that junk in your head
will disappear.

502
00:33:06,000 --> 00:33:08,040
Remember, you're someone I chose.

503
00:33:08,840 --> 00:33:11,680
Even if you don't believe in yourself,
at least believe in my judgment.

504
00:33:12,520 --> 00:33:15,040
Tomorrow when you go back to the office,
don't overthink it.

505
00:33:15,120 --> 00:33:16,360
Just go head-to-head with her.

506
00:33:16,440 --> 00:33:19,560
If you win, stop the self-punishment.

507
00:33:19,640 --> 00:33:22,280
If you lose, come learn from me.

508
00:33:22,880 --> 00:33:24,240
I'm not self-punishing.

509
00:33:25,120 --> 00:33:28,400
I'm just working off my anxiety.

510
00:33:28,480 --> 00:33:31,200
My therapist said this is a way to--

511
00:33:31,280 --> 00:33:33,760
Stop with all those weird thoughts.

512
00:33:34,600 --> 00:33:35,440
I get it.

513
00:33:36,120 --> 00:33:37,320
You think I never went
through an angsty phase?

514
00:33:44,920 --> 00:33:46,760
You can still laugh.
That means you're fine.

515
00:33:47,680 --> 00:33:48,520
Get in the car.

516
00:33:48,600 --> 00:33:49,880
I've been waiting for you long enough.

517
00:33:49,960 --> 00:33:52,040
At my age, this isn't easy.

518
00:33:56,160 --> 00:33:57,600
Don't play the victim.

519
00:33:57,680 --> 00:33:59,120
How old are you anyway?

520
00:34:01,760 --> 00:34:03,560
You're the one who said I was old.

521
00:34:03,640 --> 00:34:05,000
Said my crow's feet
were really noticeable.

522
00:34:05,520 --> 00:34:07,160
I'm keeping a running tally, you know.

523
00:34:24,480 --> 00:34:26,920
Do you go there often?

524
00:34:27,600 --> 00:34:32,679
When I'm stressed, sad,
or having nightmares.

525
00:34:33,920 --> 00:34:36,159
Someone as strong as you has nightmares?

526
00:34:36,760 --> 00:34:38,280
Everyone has their weaknesses.

527
00:34:39,280 --> 00:34:42,120
I am afraid of heights.

528
00:34:43,199 --> 00:34:44,040
Afraid of losing control.

529
00:34:44,679 --> 00:34:47,760
So whenever I go somewhere high,
I can't sleep.

530
00:34:49,560 --> 00:34:51,880
But you fly all the time…

531
00:34:51,960 --> 00:34:53,400
There's glass, so it's okay.

532
00:34:54,400 --> 00:34:56,880
Or if I'm far enough away,
it'll be better.

533
00:34:58,000 --> 00:34:58,920
Anyway,

534
00:34:59,640 --> 00:35:02,360
I think that place can heal me.

535
00:35:02,960 --> 00:35:04,240
So it can heal you too.

536
00:35:20,360 --> 00:35:21,360
Richard.

537
00:35:24,120 --> 00:35:25,400
Why do you care so much about me?

538
00:35:25,480 --> 00:35:26,840
Why do you help me so much?

539
00:35:26,920 --> 00:35:27,800
Do you…

540
00:35:31,560 --> 00:35:32,840
Do you like me?

541
00:35:47,960 --> 00:35:50,080
Can you not joke like that
when I'm driving?

542
00:35:53,600 --> 00:35:55,480
I'm not joking.

543
00:35:56,480 --> 00:35:57,560
Richard.

544
00:35:57,640 --> 00:36:00,920
I may be young,
but I'm not clueless about feelings.

545
00:36:01,000 --> 00:36:03,640
You've always been so good to me.

546
00:36:04,400 --> 00:36:05,360
I'm an adult.

547
00:36:05,440 --> 00:36:07,160
What danger could I possibly
be in in Beijing?

548
00:36:07,800 --> 00:36:10,400
You said Du was worried about me,
but I barely know him.

549
00:36:10,480 --> 00:36:12,560
So it was actually you
who was worried, right?

550
00:36:13,600 --> 00:36:18,080
If I chalked it all up
to a senior appreciating talent,

551
00:36:18,600 --> 00:36:19,920
that feels like a stretch,

552
00:36:20,000 --> 00:36:21,840
but then the other day at your apartment,

553
00:36:21,920 --> 00:36:23,880
you deliberately let me see that.

554
00:36:23,960 --> 00:36:26,120
So I'm really confused.

555
00:36:26,720 --> 00:36:27,800
But don't worry.

556
00:36:27,880 --> 00:36:31,480
I'm not asking all this to prove anything.

557
00:36:31,560 --> 00:36:32,560
I just…

558
00:36:33,400 --> 00:36:35,920
I just want to know where we stand.

559
00:36:36,520 --> 00:36:37,600
You're right.

560
00:36:38,760 --> 00:36:40,120
Of course I have feelings for you.

561
00:36:53,920 --> 00:36:58,280
If I didn't, why would I keep helping you?

562
00:37:00,160 --> 00:37:02,320
But there are many kinds of feelings.

563
00:37:02,400 --> 00:37:03,840
Not just romantic ones.

564
00:37:04,520 --> 00:37:07,080
It's like liking a celebrity.

565
00:37:07,160 --> 00:37:09,200
That doesn't mean I want to date them.

566
00:37:10,280 --> 00:37:14,040
There's a lot of gray
between black and white.

567
00:37:15,080 --> 00:37:18,240
When you interviewed,
you left a strong impression on me.

568
00:37:18,840 --> 00:37:20,960
And your personality,

569
00:37:21,040 --> 00:37:23,200
your way of thinking,
and how you handle things

570
00:37:23,720 --> 00:37:25,240
all click with mine.

571
00:37:25,960 --> 00:37:26,960
I help you

572
00:37:27,040 --> 00:37:29,880
not just because I hope you'll become
my assistant someday.

573
00:37:30,640 --> 00:37:31,680
I also want

574
00:37:32,560 --> 00:37:35,600
to make it up to my younger self
for a regret from back then.

575
00:37:36,680 --> 00:37:38,000
What regret?

576
00:37:38,680 --> 00:37:40,120
Don't tell me I look like your ex-wife.

577
00:37:43,400 --> 00:37:44,840
You watch too many dramas.

578
00:37:46,120 --> 00:37:47,680
Back when I was betrayed

579
00:37:48,640 --> 00:37:50,400
and at my lowest,

580
00:37:51,400 --> 00:37:52,600
no one

581
00:37:54,200 --> 00:37:56,360
came out of nowhere to pull me up.

582
00:37:57,640 --> 00:37:59,040
All your life,

583
00:37:59,120 --> 00:38:01,200
you fight for power,
and you toil and struggle.

584
00:38:01,280 --> 00:38:03,200
You finally make it over one small hill,

585
00:38:03,280 --> 00:38:05,960
just to have the freedom
to do what you want.

586
00:38:07,760 --> 00:38:08,880
I wasn't lucky back then.

587
00:38:08,960 --> 00:38:10,920
I never got my angel.

588
00:38:11,880 --> 00:38:13,440
Since I have that chance now,

589
00:38:14,520 --> 00:38:16,240
let me be your angel.

590
00:38:36,600 --> 00:38:38,240
POST

591
00:38:38,320 --> 00:38:41,600
<i>I have a friend</i>
<i>who met someone really good to her.</i>

592
00:38:42,960 --> 00:38:47,080
<i>But even though they said they liked her,</i>
<i>it wasn't in a romantic way.</i>

593
00:38:49,720 --> 00:38:52,520
<i>My friend says she feels</i>
<i>both calm and lost.</i>

594
00:38:53,200 --> 00:38:54,960
<i>How should I help her?</i>

595
00:38:58,200 --> 00:38:59,600
What I want to tell you is that

596
00:38:59,680 --> 00:39:05,320
I think you're a very smart
and capable girl.

597
00:39:05,920 --> 00:39:12,720
And I really enjoy working with you, too.

598
00:39:14,000 --> 00:39:15,280
You get what I mean?

599
00:39:15,360 --> 00:39:17,360
Of course. Got it. I misunderstood.

600
00:39:20,400 --> 00:39:23,840
It's just that basic appreciation.
Between people.

601
00:39:23,920 --> 00:39:25,160
You must have scored full marks

602
00:39:25,240 --> 00:39:27,680
on listening and reading
comprehension in college.

603
00:39:30,160 --> 00:39:32,800
I also scored high
on stress tolerance in my psych test.

604
00:39:33,480 --> 00:39:34,480
Really.

605
00:39:38,320 --> 00:39:39,720
HIDE FROM TAG: CLIENTS
FRIENDS: YE THE LEGEND, TINA

606
00:39:42,120 --> 00:39:44,040
KEEP THIS EDIT? DISCARD, KEEP

607
00:39:48,160 --> 00:39:49,880
DISCARD
